,{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientDataJSON"},{"type":"text","text":", validating the relying-party identifier against the configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Origin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", selecting between PIN and built-in user verification, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"processing extensions before the request reaches the authenticator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Client"},{"type":"text","text":" for any app that runs passkey ceremonies. Reach for "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directly only when you need lower-level access — raw "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeCredential"},{"type":"text","text":" \/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getAssertion"},{"type":"text","text":", credential management, or bio enrollment."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Client"},{"type":"text","text":" is an actor; a client’s lifetime is bound to the underlying "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The constructor takes four parameters that shape every ceremony:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the secure origin the client is bound to. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Origin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" enforces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the W3C secure-context rule; the client refuses to sign for relying parties whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier doesn’t match."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"isPublicSuffix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — a closure into a Public Suffix List, used to validate that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the relying-party identifier is a registrable suffix of the origin’s effective"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domain."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"enterpriseRpIds","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — relying-party identifiers allowed to receive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"platform-managed enterprise attestation. When the request specifies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/AttestationPreference\/enterprise","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", the client escalates to level 2"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(platform-managed) for RPs in this set, and uses level 1 (vendor-facilitated)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"allowedExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the set of WebAuthn extensions the client will process."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Anything the relying party requests outside this set is dropped before reaching"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the authenticator. Defaults to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Extension","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s standard set."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PIN and user verification are supplied per ceremony via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.Yu